// BiteMitra platform database schema (PostgreSQL) — Phase 0 design.
//
// Status: DESIGN. Validated with `prisma validate` and applied to an empty Postgres
// during Phase 0; the first real migration is generated in Phase 1.
// The client is generated by `prisma-client-js` into node_modules and used from plain
// JavaScript (owner directive: no TypeScript in source).
//
// Conventions (see docs/DATABASE.md):
//   * Primary keys are UUIDv7 (time-ordered → good index locality).
//   * Money is ALWAYS integer paise (`*Paise`, Int). Never Float/Decimal-as-float.
//     Ledger running balances and settlement totals use BigInt paise.
//   * Rates are integer basis points (`*Bps`; 1% = 100 bps, 12.5% = 1250 bps).
//   * Distances are integer metres (`*M`), durations integer seconds/minutes as named.
//   * Coordinates are Decimal(9,6) (≈0.1 m precision).
//   * Commercial rules are immutable versions: an "edit" closes the current row
//     (`effectiveTo`) and inserts a new row pointing at it via `supersedesId`.
//     That table *is* the configuration history (spec §63).
//   * Orders copy every applied value into OrderPricingSnapshot / OrderItem columns
//     so later configuration changes never alter historical orders (spec §27).

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

